** params: 16 free + 0 frozen knobs (sizing.yaml) · 6 tied · 0 ratio-derived (abstract/params.yaml) · 4 testbench params
** AUTHORED TEMPLATE — amplifier/tran_step_biaswrap: unity-gain step settling for DUTs on the
** AnalogGym self-bias convention (ports vss vdd vinn vinp vout; NO ibias port). Single-ended
** companion of tran_step_diff (M4 follow-up). Unlike the AC/noise bias-wraps — which AC-open the
** loop with Lfb/Cin — a settling measurement WANTS the real closed loop: wire the inverting input
** directly to the output (unity-gain follower) and step the non-inverting input. Settle to the
** FINAL output value, not the input step, so a systematic offset can't hold a fixed-tolerance band
** open forever (see universal/tran_step for the rationale). These are compensated multistage OTAs,
** designed stable in unity feedback.
**
** Assumes the AnalogGym canonical DUT port order (self-biased; NO ibias port):
**   .subckt <id> vss vdd vinn vinp vout
** Bindings: DUT VDD VCM CL VSTEP TSTART TSTEP TSTOP VTOL PDK_INCLUDE.
** FIXED 2026-07-20: this template used to hardcode `X1 0 vdd opout_dc opin opout amp_033_ti_ldo_ref_selfbias`,
** which silently assumed the AnalogGym port order [vss vdd vinn vinp vout] and MIS-WIRED any
** DUT declaring a different order (e.g. the amplifier-class [vdd vout vinp vinn vss] swaps
** vdd<->vss). It now uses XDUT vdd vout vinp vinn vss with canonical node names, exactly like the
** *_biaswrap_ibias sibling. For the AnalogGym DUTs this is a no-op: their vss port binds to
** node `vss`, which `Vss vss 0 dc 0` ties to ground just as the old direct-to-0 wiring did.
.lib tsmc_n65_models.scs tt
.temp 27

.param VDD=1.2
.param VCM=0.291
.param CL=10p
.param VSTEP=0.1

Vdd  vdd 0 dc {VDD}
Vss  vss 0 dc 0
CLoad vout 0 {CL}
Vinp vinp 0 dc {VCM} pulse({VCM} {VCM+VSTEP} 1u 1n 1n 1 1)
Vfb  vinn vout dc 0          ; unity-gain feedback wire (vinn <- vout; 0 V source = ideal wire)

XDUT vdd vout vinp vinn vss amp_033_ti_ldo_ref_selfbias
.control
  set filetype=ascii
  tran 1n 2u
  * settle to the FINAL value, not the input step — a follower's systematic offset would
  * otherwise keep |vout - vfinal| outside a tight tolerance band forever.
  meas tran vfinal FIND v(vout) AT=2u
  let verr = abs(v(vout) - vfinal)
  meas tran tcross WHEN verr=1m FALL=LAST
  let t_settle = tcross - 1u
  print t_settle
  write
  quit
.endc
.param x_dut_xmbp_w=10.844u
.param x_dut_xmbp_l=2u
.param x_dut_xmb0_w=12u
.param x_dut_xmb0_l=2u
.param x_dut_xmbc_w=8.316u
.param x_dut_xmbc_m=1
.param x_dut_xmbo_w=4u
.param x_dut_xmbo_m=1
.param x_dut_xm1_w=86.42u
.param x_dut_xm1_l=0.7u
.param x_dut_xm3_w=20u
.param x_dut_xm3_l=1u
.param x_dut_xm5_w=37.76u
.param x_dut_xm5_l=2.646u
.param r_z=30.853k
.param c_comp=4.508p
